From 4485ad77c9e58d3c7922e84cca656e4c7cf74231 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 22:20:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v18.6.0 Show, Don't Tell + v18.7.0 The Hall of Fame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two releases in one commit — the cloud container this work was done in had
no git history to commit against incrementally, so both are landing together.

v18.6.0 — Show, Don't Tell
- Move buttons become type-coloured tiles with a big type symbol; the move
  name is demoted to a caption. Junior mode enlarges the symbol further.
- impactFx(): one visual grammar for what a hit did. Super-effective is a
  red chevron, hard shake and oversized number; not-very is a small grey
  chevron; immune is a grey X with no particles and no number; a crit is a
  white flash-frame plus starburst.
- Fainted sprites grey out and tip over; HP bars pulse below 20%.
- Replace both window.prompt() nickname calls with an in-world panel.
  prompt() is suppressed in an installed iOS PWA — it returns null without
  throwing, so nicknames never worked on the boys' iPad at all.
- inkFor() picks chip ink by measuring contrast instead of hardcoding white.
  All 18 type colours now clear WCAG AA (worst 4.73:1, previously ~1.4:1).

v18.7.0 — The Hall of Fame
- Persist champion:{date, team, levels} in the save, written once so a later
  completion never overwrites the day it first happened. Import-validated.
- Fullscreen Hall of Fame: six sprites march on one at a time with a rising
  beep each, confetti, four-note fanfare, no timer. Released by teardown so
  the ceremony can't deadlock the victory path behind a hidden modal.
- Permanent crown on the trainer card.
- Fix a smoke assertion that had been green by luck since v18.5: it checked
  wild levels against a +/-20% multiplicative band, but v18.5 replaced that
  with the additive habitat leash. The engine was always right. The leash is
  now covered exhaustively in engine.test.mjs.

134 browser checks, 18 engine unit tests, four consecutive clean runs.

